## Auth

`useAuth()` (from `src/auth/AuthContext.jsx`) talks to the exact JWT contract the backend composer's `auth-jwt*` modules expose: `POST /auth/{register,login,refresh,logout}`, `GET /auth/me`. The access token is kept in memory only; the refresh token is an httpOnly cookie the browser sends automatically (`credentials: "include"` in `src/auth/authApi.js`) — a page reload silently re-authenticates via that cookie, nothing is ever put in localStorage.

```jsx
import { useAuth } from "@/auth/AuthContext";
import { Button, Spinner } from "@/components";
import { LoginForm } from "@/components/LoginForm";

function Profile() {
  const { user, loading, logout } = useAuth();
  if (loading) return <Spinner />;
  if (!user) return <LoginForm />;
  return (
    <>
      <p>Signed in as {user.email}</p>
      <Button onClick={logout}>Log out</Button>
    </>
  );
}
```

`LoginForm` / `RegisterForm` / `AuthStatus` in `src/components/` are ready-made — `AuthStatus` is the pattern above, already wired together, and is what's dropped into `src/App.jsx` by default.

Set `VITE_API_URL` in `.env` to point at your backend (defaults to `http://localhost:4000/api/v1`, matching the backend composer's default). If your backend runs on a different origin than this frontend's dev server, also set `CORS_ORIGIN` on the *backend* to match this app's URL — the backend composer's CORS setup only allows one specific origin plus credentials, by design (a wildcard origin can't be paired with credentialed requests at all).

